      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nSibling of #31537; prerequisite of #30877 (enable STANDALONE + DP attention).\r\n\r\nCurrent idle DP ranks hardcode the target-verify capture mode to `FULL`, but STANDALONE's verify graph is captured with `NULL` (draft model is independent). So an idle rank falls back to eager while the active ranks run the graph. Ranks diverging on graph-vs-eager cause a **collective deadlock**. This PR makes `forward_batch` the source of truth and sets idle `spec_info` capture mode to`NULL`, so it never escalates beyond what `forward_batch` actually requests.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- `EagleVerifyInput.create_idle_input()`: make `capture_hidden_mode` a required arg instead of hardcoding `FULL` so every idle call site states its mode explicitly.\r\n- `build_eagle_verify_input()`: on the idle path, pass `NULL` so `requested = max(fb, spec_info)` collapses back to `fb`, matching active path.\r\n- `_build_trivial_verify_input()` (behavior is **unchanged**): on the idle path, pass `FULL` to align with active path.\r\n\r\n**NOTE:** `_build_trivial_verify_input()` is touched only to satisfy the required argument; both its idle and active paths use `FULL` and already agree. If STANDALONE ever supports `steps == 0`, both sides should move to the algorithm-derived mode together in a follow-up.\r\n\r\n## Unit Tests\r\n\r\nRuntime path (STANDALONE + DP attention) is gated on main, so coverage is a CPU unit test asserting the idle path of `build_eagle_verify_input()` returns the enum floor `NULL` regardless of algorithm; so it never raises capture mode above what `forward_batch` decides.\r\n\r\n### Before (pre-fix): idle returns `FULL`, the test fails\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1690\" height=\"936\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-18 at 10 00 52 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/731de734-2801-43cb-882c-ded5143dade5\" />\r\n\r\n### After (this PR): idle returns `NULL`, the test passes\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1900\" height=\"270\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-18 at 9 59 04 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e4438322-2656-4be3-83c9-bcec1b21cb19\" />\r\n\r\n## E2E Test\r\n\r\nDP ranks diverging on graph-vs-eager, triggered by reverting this fix in STANDALONE + DP attention support:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1149\" height=\"135\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3a71677e-9882-461e-b03b-8cab63f3a1ad\" />\r\n\r\nWith this fix, all ranks agree:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1136\" height=\"139\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/af190cfb-3793-49f6-ac95-d8af6279462b\" />\r\n\r\nFor full E2E test, please refer to #30877.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nDeferred to #30877, where STANDALONE + DP attention is enabled.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nOut of scope; this PR focuses on correctness only.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #29805568593](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/29805568593)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #29805568447](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/29805568447)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
